==English==

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[bite off]] [[more]] [[than]] [[one]] [[can]] [[chew]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To try to do too much; to [[take on]] or [[attempt]] more than one is capable of doing.
#: ''I think I '''bit off more than I could chew''' when I agreed to paint this house by myself.''

====Usage notes====
* Often used as a caution, "don't bite off more than you can chew".

